NOVA X native desktop package
==============================

The launcher is /usr/bin/nova-x. It opens a native PySide6/Qt window and does
not start a browser or web server. `nova-x diagnostics` prints local setup
checks, and `nova-x exec -- PROGRAM ARG...` runs a structured local command.

The application runs as the logged-in user. It does not store sudo passwords,
start a daemon, or listen on a network port. Privileged task actions use pkexec
and the system polkit agent only after a separate NOVA approval.

Provider keys are stored in the logged-in desktop's Secret Service keyring. A
working and unlocked Secret Service provider is required to save keys. If the
keyring is unavailable, NOVA refuses plaintext fallbacks. Chat and task model
requests are not sent until the user explicitly submits work or starts a test.

Per-user data is stored under $XDG_DATA_HOME/nova-x (normally
~/.local/share/nova-x); the default workspace is ~/NOVA-X-workspace. SQLite and
NOVA-created command logs are private to the account. Extra workspace paths
must be deliberately selected in the application.

Scheduled/background operation, a continuously running service, desktop
automation, microphone access, and self-modification are not implemented by
this package. Tasks stop when the app exits. Diagnostics do not make network
requests.

This package was built and its metadata, extracted tree, Python imports/syntax,
and non-GUI CLI execution were checked in a Debian 13 sandbox. The sandbox had
no active desktop, keyring, polkit agent, or PySide6 installation, so the Qt
window, Secret Service unlock flow, privileged actions, and installation on a
Kali host were not exercised here. Confirm package compatibility and install
only on the intended Kali machine.
